# Line endings
# The repository stores every text file with LF. On checkout, text files follow the platform (core.autocrlf /
# core.eol: CRLF on Windows, LF elsewhere), so editors and the build see native line endings and no file shows up
# as changed only because of its line endings.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must keep LF on every platform, or bash fails on the carriage returns.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows scripts are always checked out with CRLF (cmd.exe and Windows PowerShell 5.1 expect it).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Solution files: Visual Studio rewrites them with CRLF.
*.sln text eol=crlf

# Binary content
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.dmp binary
